  },
  "articleBody": "It's frustrating to see your bathroom paint peeling, bubbling, or even growing mildew. This usually points to one main culprit: moisture. Bathrooms are high-humidity zones, and if you're not using the right kind of paint or preparing the surfaces properly, that moisture will cause problems. A big mistake is using **non-moisture-resistant paint**. Regular wall paint just isn't formulated to stand up to steamy showers and high humidity; it'll quickly start to break down. Another common issue is failing to properly **clean and de-gloss existing surfaces** before painting. If the walls are dirty, greasy, or too glossy, the new paint won't adhere well and will peel off. Also, skipping **primer** on patched areas or places where mildew was present means those issues can bleed through your new topcoats. And finally, if you're painting before other elements like flooring or trim are installed, it can lead to rework or irregular joints. Taking the time for proper prep and using quality, bathroom-specific paint makes all the difference. If you're struggling with persistent peeling, HH Remodeling LLC can help diagnose the underlying issue and get your bathroom looking great again.",
